From d58fbb8cfc587323f8c72584cf216b2827f57f5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TOKITA Hiroshi <tokita.hiroshi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Jun 2025 09:07:46 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] include: zephyr: xen: public: remove and migrate to the `zephyr-xenlib`

This PR migrates the MIT-licensed Xen public headers into the
`include/zephyr/xen/public` directory to the zephyr-xenlib module.

Since the xen public headers require GCC extensions,
enable GNU_C_EXTENSIONS along with enabling CONFIG_XEN.

Backported to Zephyr v4.4.1: v4.4.1 was cut from the v4.4 maintenance branch
(forked at v4.4.0, 2026-04-14) and does not contain this commit. Four things
differ from the upstream commit:

 - drivers/xen/gnttab.c: upstream carries `#include <zephyr/xen/regions.h>` as an
   unchanged context line, added there by some later commit on main. v4.4.1 has no
   such line, and gnttab.c uses nothing from that header, so it is NOT added here.
   An earlier revision of this patch did add it, which stopped the patch being a
   straight backport and created a bogus ordering dependency on 0023.

 - doc/releases/migration-guide-4.5.rst: the upstream hunk anchors on a WiFi entry
   that does not exist in v4.4.1, where the 4.5 guide is still an empty skeleton.
   The same six lines therefore go into the empty zephyr-keep-sorted block
   instead. The wording is upstream's, verbatim.

 - include/zephyr/xen/gnttab.h additionally gains <stdbool.h> and <stdint.h>.
   Upstream did not add them in this commit because an earlier one already had; on
   v4.4.1 the bool/uintN_t it uses arrived transitively through the vendored
   <zephyr/xen/public/grant_table.h> being replaced here, so without them the header
   no longer compiles standalone.

 - the 14 header deletions under include/zephyr/xen/public/ are performed by
   apply-zephyr-patches.sh (rm -rf) rather than by this patch: the reset loop that
   runs before it restores tracked files, so a deletion hunk would be undone on
   every re-run and this patch would then fail its forward check.

Signed-off-by: TOKITA Hiroshi <tokita.hiroshi@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/commit/d58fbb8cfc587323f8c72584cf216b2827f57f5e]
---
